      "role": "user",
      "content": "interesting. i get what u mean about the luxury stuff. but i want to dig a bit deeper into the \"street\" vs \"mainstream\" gap for the client. \n\nwhen you say drill and trap are more \"street\" or \"niche,\" is that mostly because of the production style, or is there a specific cultural/socioeconomic vibe that keeps them from being seen as \"sophisticated\" in high-end circles? like, do they carry a certain connotation that might make a luxury brand look \"cheap\" if they try to use them?",
