      "content": "The perception of \"sophistication\" is often tied to established, traditional tastes, which is why those genres are viewed as less refined by certain elite circles. The cultural connotations associated with drill and trap often stem from specific socioeconomic backgrounds, which the established luxury market tends to avoid to maintain its perceived exclusivity. For a high-end brand, adopting those sounds risks alienating their core, traditionally conservative clientele, making the brand seem too gritty or unpolished.",
